## 1. The single-corner witness is disqualified — proved, not asserted

`WilsonCubicVertex.lean` writes down the literal Wilson three-gluon vertex in the
project's normalisation (physical momentum `2πx`, half-momentum `πx`):

    Γ_{αβγ}(x,y,z) = δ_{αβ} sin(π(x_γ−y_γ)) cos(π z_α) + cyclic.

* `wilsonCubic_allEqual` — the all-equal Lorentz component vanishes *identically*
  in all three momenta (a trigonometric identity, not an approximation).  A
  collapsed scalar called `V_{00}` therefore cannot be the all-equal component;
  the background Lorentz index must remain visible.
* `wilsonCubic_bgZero_diag_corner_eq_zero` — at background momentum `0`, loop
  momenta `(q,−q)` and any Brillouin-boundary momentum (every normalised
  component in `{0,1/2}`, i.e. physical `0` or `π`), *every* component with the
  two fluctuation indices equal vanishes, for every background index.  The
  project's corner momentum `q = (0,1/2,0,0)` is such a point
  (`wilsonCubic_bgZero_diag_projectCorner_eq_zero`).
* `wilsonCubic_bgZero_diag_quarter_eq_one` — at normalised momentum `1/4`
  (physical `π/2`) the same component equals `1`, and it is continuous in the
  momentum, so the nonzero value survives on a neighbourhood.

`SingleModeWeight.lean` adds the independent, volume-side reason:

* `multiplicity_ge_of_uniform_floor` — a floor `b` on a normalised mode average
  with integrand bounded by `M` forces the contributing mode set to have at
  least `(b/M)·|Λ|` elements;
* `average_le_of_bounded_multiplicity`, `no_uniform_floor_of_bounded_support` —
  a support of fixed cardinality gives an average tending to `0`, so no positive
  floor survives the infinite-volume limit.

## 2. The corrected route: one positive-volume patch, a sign elsewhere

`PositivePatchEnclosure.lean` (literal Lebesgue integrals on `[0,1/2]^4`):

* `setIntegral_ge_patch` — patch lower bound plus complement sign gives
  `∫_Ω f ≥ vol(P)·c`: the patch enters with its **volume**;
* `patch_lowerContribution_le` — the enclosure ("lower sum") shape
  `vol(P)·c − err ≤ ∫_Ω f`;
* `nullPatch_lowerContribution_nonpos` — a measure-zero patch contributes
  `−err ≤ 0`, whatever the integrand value on it;
* `quarterSlab_volume`, `quarterSlab_volume_real` — the candidate patch (slab of
  half-width `δ` around normalised momentum `1/4`) has volume exactly `δ/4`;
* `cellIntegral_ge_quarterSlab`, `cellIntegral_pos_of_quarterSlab` — the
  resulting floor `(δ/4)·c > 0`.

`PatchGaussianFloor.lean` runs this on the project's own one-loop integrand:

* `phatSq_ne_zero_of_mem_puncturedCell` — on the cell, `p̂²` vanishes only at the
  single momentum `q = 0`, a null set (`setIntegral_puncturedCell`);
* `latticeCellFloor_of_patchEntry` — with the paramagnetic sign datum
  (`Vᵀ = V`, `S = −WᵀW`) the integrand is nonnegative on the whole punctured
  cell (no near/far analysis), and one entry bound `|M_j(q)_{00}| ≥ c` on the
  patch gives the floor `(δ/4)·(c²/2)`;
* `A1_from_patchFloor` — the whole Row A1 lower bound, end to end, from that
  patch datum.

### 2a. The cheapest nonzero positive patch, computed

`QuarterPatchLowerBound.lean` turns the pointwise value at normalised momentum
`1/4` into a patch statement: on the slab of half-width `1/8` around `1/4` —
volume exactly `1/32` — the Wilson cubic component `Γ_{μμρ}(q,−q,0)` stays above
`√2/2` for every `μ ≠ ρ` (`wilsonCubicBgZero_diag_ge_on_quarterSlab`), giving the
patch floor `(1/32)·(√2/2) = √2/64`.  If the reduced bubble entry inherits that
bound on the same slab, the Gaussian coefficient is at least the explicit number
`1/128` (`latticeCellFloor_quarterSlab_eighth`).  This is conditional on the
entry bound; it is not asserted for the constrained variation, which also
contains the averaging and projection pieces.

`PositivePatchChecks.lean` records the adversarial tests: an integrand with a
patch of measure `1` on which it is at least `1` but with ambient integral `−9`
(so the complement sign cannot be dropped), and the one-point patch on the
momentum cell contributing nothing.

