## 5. The constrained first variation keeps all its indices

`FirstVariationDecomposition.lean` fixes `V_constrained = W + Q + R` (Wilson
Hessian variation, averaging-operator variation, gauge/constrained projection
variation) as a fully index-resolved symbol
`V_{αβ;ρ}^{ab;c}(q)`, and proves:

* `wilsonPiece_allEqual_zero`, `wilsonPiece_diag_corner_zero` — the `W` piece
  vanishes on the all-equal component and on the whole diagonal at corner
  momenta;
* `component_ne_zero_imp` — a nonzero component of `V` forces one of `W,Q,R` to
  be nonzero there;
* `wilsonPiece_positive_but_total_zero` — an explicit `V` whose `W` piece is
  strictly positive at a momentum while `W+Q+R` vanishes there: the `Q` and `R`
  variations may not be assumed to vanish;
* `patchBound_of_wilson_and_remainder` — the correct compiler: a lower bound `c`
  on `W` over the patch plus a bound `e` on `|Q|+|R|` there gives `c − e` for
  `V`, which is exactly what the patch enclosure consumes.

## 6. Audit: a "universal coefficient" field is not a derivation

`UniversalCoefficientCircularity.lean` models a carrier with the field
`infraredCoefficient = universalColorCoefficient` and proves:

* `coefficient_of_universalField` — the value follows *from the field*;
* `universalField_uninformative` — every integrand can be carried with every
  value, so the field constrains nothing about the literal integrand;
* `coefficient_not_determined_by_integrand`,
  `universalField_consistent_with_zero_integrand` — the coefficient is not a
  function of the integrand, and a value such as `11/12` is consistent with an
  identically vanishing integrand;
* `coefficient_determined_of_derived` — the contrast: a coefficient equal to a
  fixed functional of the integrand *is* determined.  That is the shape a
  genuine extraction must have.

Accordingly, no theorem in this development uses such a carrier as an input to
the Gaussian floor.

